{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01F2iJGxZuD3pDSkNnhnP6hY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Anchor R&D Surface v2 â€” Master Plan (Planning Session Summary)\n\n**Goal (North Star, locked)**\n- Make Anchor's R&D surface a **truthful, useful memory** of each project's trio work.\n- **Imported history is first-class history:** a brownfield-discovered trio run counts as real project history, not a second-class `import` placeholder. An honest \"imported\" provenance chip is acceptable, but lane status must reflect actual *activity* rather than masquerade it as empty.\n- **One trio run = one session:** a research/plan/build run is presented as a single *session* read as a clean summary, not as N separate per-file cards.\n\n**Key design decisions**\n- **Interactive terminal substrate = stream-json REPL (not ConPTY).** A true ConPTY terminal needs a native dependency, which violates Anchor's stdlib-only / no-compiled-assets rule. v2 instead keeps the terminal *feel* over a **persistent `stream-json` REPL**: one long-lived `claude`/`gemini` process per session, user turns POSTed to stdin, assistant output streamed back via **SSE** (replacing the prior 1.5s poll).\n- The REPL **generalizes the existing gate-stdin mechanism**, **auto-seeds the right skill per lane**, and on process exit **auto-discovers produced files** and asks the user to confirm adoption as a session.\n- Terminal console rendering was vendored like KaTeX already is (offline, no compiled assets).\n\n**Follow-up decision â€” real xterm.js swap (user: GO, 2026-06-11)**\n- User chose **real xterm.js** over the lightweight anchor-term console.\n- Execution: vendored **`@xterm/xterm 6.0.0`** (offline copy, MIT LICENSE + PROVENANCE) into `vendor/xterm/`; rewrote `vendor/anchor-term/anchor-term.js` as an **adapter** over `new window.Terminal(...)` preserving the same `window.AnchorTerm.mount` API, gates, discoverâ†’adopt panel, and beforeunload reap; added a traversal-safe `/vendor/xterm/` static route + includes (xterm loaded before anchor-term).\n- Backend `rnd_terminal.py` and the SSE/term endpoints were **byte-unchanged** (verified via empty git diff).\n- **Gate (orchestrator-run): 394 passed** (claim truncated in source: \"1 sâ€¦\" â€” exact skip/timing figure not fully captured in the provided anchor).\n\n**Member documents**\n- Anchor R&D Surface v2 â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n- Anchor R&D Surface v2 â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n- Anchor R&D Surface v2 â€” Execution Log\n\n---\n*Note: one anchor (the xterm.js gate result) is truncated in the source material at \"394 passed, 1 sâ€¦\", so the full gate figure is not grounded here.*"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3aded867-b183-4a0a-8a75-c3b28ae69e52","uuid":"e2253daa-facd-424c-ac9d-045b9864853c","request_id":"req_011Cc1JNQeKfsnVMpcFN39wx"}
